<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate falls in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate falls in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate fell in this week's primary auction and demand rose, Banco de Mexico said.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	19.69	    -176	    19.65     19.75</p>
<p>91-Day	22.14	    -107	    22.05     22.20</p>
<p>182-Day     22.75	    -131	    22.65     22.85</p>
<p>356-Day     23.99				23.84     24.10</p>
<p>Last week the 363-day paper was assigned at 25.30 pct.</p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	900 million pesos   3.92 bln pesos     4.36</p>
<p>91-Day	900 million pesos   4.01 bln pesos     4.46</p>
<p>182-Day     900 million pesos   3.16 bln pesos     3.51</p>
<p>356-Day     600 million pesos   2.27 bln pesos     3.78</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 4.05 on demand of 13.36 billion pesos compared with 3.85 the week before, on demand of 12.72 billion pesos the week before.</p>
<p>Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			    6 basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			    6 basis points</p>
<p>    182-Day			  10 basis points</p>
<p>    356-Day			  11 basis points</p>
<p>((-- Robert Kozak, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
